ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"f33d3ffcb47ac6c2fc8f1048d93dc84c33139ffb0fbd9d17c41390ba1a818296","event_uuid":"61976199-d698-4438-a495-0a6390ec7757","position":{"commit_sha":"44740999a45adb23012c2493f58ebf7bdb9c1b27","position":"1787815573938003146-61976199-d698-4438-a495-0a6390ec7757"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"4f3332f82a98a4a2445524fbb1cde5bda0a10d09f5794c552fbd66421a245380","event_uuid":"054134ef-7e3a-4846-bda9-7ca046e0cf66","position":{"commit_sha":"44740999a45adb23012c2493f58ebf7bdb9c1b27","position":"1787815738422559670-054134ef-7e3a-4846-bda9-7ca046e0cf66"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"787d09b851bf1bc9cd33830f4ee8033d6a29628c3272c8432de1a703dac65832","event_uuid":"af8b2c05-0c68-43cf-a1c9-f19fee351b8b","position":{"commit_sha":"44740999a45adb23012c2493f58ebf7bdb9c1b27","position":"1787815748032853830-af8b2c05-0c68-43cf-a1c9-f19fee351b8b"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Second independent victim of the same missing-.git mechanism, observed on the same live server:\n\n    reconcile {\"mode\": \"dry-run\"}\n      -> {\"error\": \"command_failed\",\n          \"message\": \"reconcile (dry-run) failed (exit 1): ERROR: reconciler process failed\n           before finalization: Command '['git', '-C', '/app', 'hash-object', '-w',\n           '--stdin']' returned non-zero exit status 128.\"}\n\nreconcile dry-run is documented as non-mutating and always available, and it fails for the same\nreason as review_plan/verify_completion: /app has no git object DB, so \nexits 128. This widens the blast radius beyond the LLM gates and is covered by AC4 (a real git\nobject DB at the repo root) and AC5 (a deploy-time health check).","timestamp":1787815565502359559},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Third victim of the same missing-.git mechanism, same live server:\n\n    review_code {\"base\": \"HEAD~1\", \"head\": \"HEAD\"}\n      -> {\"error\": \"llm_unavailable\",\n          \"message\": \"git diff HEAD~1...HEAD failed: warning: Not a git repository.\n           Use --no-index to compare two paths outside a working tree ...\"}\n\nConfirmed blast radius on the deployed server, all from /app having no git object DB:\n  - review_plan       (default attested source) - fails\n  - verify_completion (default attested source) - fails\n  - review_code                                  - fails\n  - reconcile         (dry-run, documented non-mutating/always-available) - fails\n  - attach_commits                               - cannot resolve any SHA\nOnly source=local variants run, and a local verdict is never signed.","timestamp":1787815738422559670}],"created_at":1787815136989669529,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"2235fcfa-36c7-480f-8f56-ff1dcb5ff0ad","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"1f19-adf2-ffb2-4b09"},{"link_uuid":"61976199-d698-4438-a495-0a6390ec7757","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"c67b-ece5-707e-460e"},{"link_uuid":"af8b2c05-0c68-43cf-a1c9-f19fee351b8b","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"d26a-8ffa-97cd-4b2a"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\nEvery **attested-source** LLM gate operation fails on the LIVE MCP server\n(`https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/mcp`, container `compose-mcp-1`, image\n`compose-mcp:9499312eb7b05dc3d75d39c23ab74a5b4afc26b5`).\n\nObserved 2026-08-27 against the live endpoint:\n\n```\nreview_plan       {\"ticket_id\": \"ruby-griffinish-goitered\"}\n  -> Error executing tool review_plan: cannot resolve ref 'origin/main' to a commit in '.'.\nreview_plan       {\"ticket_id\": \"...\", \"ref\": \"HEAD\"}\n  -> Error executing tool review_plan: cannot resolve ref 'HEAD' to a commit in '.'.\nverify_completion {\"ticket_id\": \"...\"}\n  -> Error executing tool verify_completion: cannot resolve ref 'origin/main' to a commit in '.'.\nreview_plan       {\"ticket_id\": \"...\", \"source\": \"local\"}   -> RUNS (P1/P2/P3 emitted)\n```\n\n## Mechanism\nThe container's repo root has **no git metadata at all**. Verified in-container:\n\n```\n$ docker exec compose-mcp-1 sh -c 'pwd; ls -d /app/.git; git -C /app rev-parse origin/main'\n/app\nls: cannot access '/app/.git': No such file or directory\nfatal: not a git repository (or any of the parent directories): .git\n```\n\n`docker inspect` confirms `WorkingDir=/app`, `Cmd=[\"rebar-mcp\"]`, and the env carries\n`REBAR_TRACKER_DIR=/var/gerrit/site/mcp-tickets` but **no `REBAR_ROOT`** \u2014 so the repo root\nresolves to the cwd `/app`, which is a plain source copy, not a work tree. The image ships\n`/app/.deployed_ref` (`d4a0a2a44 (feat/gerrit-ci-verified-gate)`) as a text marker instead of a\nreal clone. `source=attested` pins a snapshot at `ref` against that root's object DB, so ref\nresolution fails before any LLM call.\n\nThe tracker itself is unaffected: it is an out-of-tree clone reached via `REBAR_TRACKER_DIR`,\nso all non-git tools (create/show/search/list/comment/edit/link/claim/transition) work.\n\n## Impact\n`attested` is the DEFAULT source for both gate ops, and a `local`-source verdict is never\nsigned. So **no plan-review or completion attestation can be earned through the live MCP\nserver**, and consequently no `task`/`story`/`epic` can be closed through it while\n`verify.require_plan_review_for_close` is on \u2014 the only remaining path is `--force`, which\nagents are prohibited from using. Reproduced live: probe task `ruby-griffinish-goitered`\n(`c67b-ece5-707e-460e`) is stuck `in_progress` with\n`plan-review close gate: unsigned: no certified plan-review attestation`, and the prescribed\nremedy (`review-plan`) is the very operation that cannot run.\n\n## Reproduction\n1. Call `review_plan` on any claimable ticket through the live MCP endpoint with default args.\n2. Observe `cannot resolve ref 'origin/main' to a commit in '.'`.\n3. Repeat with `source: \"local\"` and observe it runs.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] AC1: `review_plan` with default arguments against the deployed MCP server returns a plan-review verdict (PASS/BLOCK/INDETERMINATE) rather than a ref-resolution error.\n- [ ] AC2: `verify_completion` with default arguments likewise returns a completion verdict.\n- [ ] AC3: A PASS from AC1 persists a signed plan-review attestation, so `plan_review_status` on that ticket reports `certified`.\n- [ ] AC4: The deployed container exposes a git object DB for the repo root reachable by the gate ops (a real clone at the repo root, or an explicit `REBAR_ROOT` pointing at one), verified by `git -C <root> rev-parse origin/main` succeeding inside the container.\n- [ ] AC5: A deploy-time health check fails the deploy when the repo root cannot resolve the configured attested base ref, so this cannot regress silently.\n\n## Definition of Done\n- [ ] DD1: AC1-AC3 demonstrated against a deployed MCP server.\n- [ ] DD2: AC5 check runs in the deploy path (compose/entrypoint or autodeploy) and is covered by a test.\n","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[["relates_to","c67b-ece5-707e-460e"],["relates_to","d26a-8ffa-97cd-4b2a"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":["mcp","deploy","gates"],"ticket_id":"1eb6-65f2-5a4e-4c7b","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Attested-source LLM gates are unusable on the deployed MCP server: the container repo root has no git metadata","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["2f038111-8f97-4a12-9cc1-195b34122b0d","2235fcfa-36c7-480f-8f56-ff1dcb5ff0ad","8540459e-21dd-4d3a-a340-e507fbcff96d","61976199-d698-4438-a495-0a6390ec7757","054134ef-7e3a-4846-bda9-7ca046e0cf66","af8b2c05-0c68-43cf-a1c9-f19fee351b8b"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787821809019629924,"uuid":"b9391f47-d882-4f89-a198-43db921231c9"}
